  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Market study in Cartagena</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aiming for a long-term collaboration with the City of Cartagena through the programme Water as Leverage (WaL), executed by Partners for Water, the Netherlands government developed an initiative to kick-start and create scalable sustainable solutions for climate adaptation challenges.WaL Cartagena supports sustainable, resilient economic development in Cartagena city, in line with key policy instruments of the district municipality, like the &quot;Plan 4C: Competitive and Climate Compatible Cartagena&quot;.This partnership between the Netherlands and Cartagena is key in answering the need for more investments in resilient water-related infrastructure and an opportunity to leverage competitive and sustainable local economic development, where the local economic actors play a key role.Now, the intention is to build upon the Water as Leverage programme for the &quot;combi-track approach&quot; proposal &apos;Cartagena ABC&apos;. To successfully develop the proposal, it is key to foster not only climate solutions and local development, but also opportunities for Dutch business, and business to business opportunities with local partners.This market study will serve to analyse these opportunities in a coherent matter, complementary to the Water as Leverage approach.</narrative>
  </description>
